WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:00.913
- Does it make?

00:00:00.913 --> 00:00:02.511
Oh yes they love this.

00:00:02.511 --> 00:00:04.678
(squeaks)

00:00:04.889 --> 00:00:07.556
(playful music)

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:24.170
2015, Party, 'cause that was a party

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:27.443
and my absolute favorite
song would have to be,

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:31.503
Into the New World 'cause
that's what started the story.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:41.530
Over my Skin is for everyone
about finally being comfortable

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.510
in your own skin.

00:00:42.510 --> 00:00:46.310
I wanted to bring all the
things I love about K-pop

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:49.770
and all the things I love
about the pop I grew up to

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:53.980
and for an album, yes,
I'm hoping to continuously

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:57.790
put out music and hopefully
have a body of work

00:00:57.790 --> 00:00:59.153
to share for my fans.

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:08.560
There was like Fannytastics,
friends here were like,

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.540
we can call them Fannypacks.

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:12.690
I was like oh my god no.

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.160
But there are some really
really fun and creative names

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:18.070
so I'm really looking
forward to what the fans

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:18.983
come up with.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.550
So, let me know what you guys think.

00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:22.603
Don't say Fannypack.

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:28.137
I'm a huge fan of the Lionheart Talk Talk

00:01:28.330 --> 00:01:30.650
because I had a lot of
input on that album.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:33.560
That song, I loved so
much, that I performed

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.720
at my solo concert like
on an acoustic version.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:39.043
Sorry to disappoint but,

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:41.600
nope, actually they
said, if she doesn't pick

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:44.450
the Lionheart Talk
Talk, we don't know her.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.673
So yes, you do know me.

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:52.603
The tour outfit and I feel
like everybody's like yes.

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:55.100
That was not the pink we
thought we were getting.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.830
And then it was like fluorescent

00:01:57.571 --> 00:02:00.913
almost obnoxious pink.

00:02:01.044 --> 00:02:03.544
(jazzy music)

00:02:05.950 --> 00:02:08.605
Everything is a challenge but growing up

00:02:08.605 --> 00:02:11.410
in front of the camera, my
band mates and I were talking

00:02:11.410 --> 00:02:13.560
about certain things
and then they're like,

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:15.794
wow we coped really well
and I was like, yeah,

00:02:15.794 --> 00:02:18.280
a pat on the back to everybody.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.730
Growing up would probably be
one of the toughest things

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:21.563
but I'm here.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:24.183
At this interview, I made it.

00:02:25.168 --> 00:02:26.790
(soft music)

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:30.190
I feel like I'd probably
be doing the art side

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:34.300
or the behind the scenes side to music

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:39.300
or fashion or puppies or, (laughs)

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:43.130
I guess I'm getting both worlds

00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:46.600
where I get to come here and
say I'm thinking in Korean

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.490
because I was always thinking in English

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:52.763
when I was in Korea but I
guess I'm flexing both muscles.

00:02:54.636 --> 00:02:57.100
(playful music)

00:02:57.100 --> 00:03:00.740
my secret is having just
as comfortable shoes

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.460
when I'm off of 'em and balancing,

00:03:03.460 --> 00:03:05.933
'cause you can yes, it's unreal.

00:03:06.153 --> 00:03:08.085
My choreographers unreal.

00:03:08.085 --> 00:03:10.168
(laughs)

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:13.503
Mind control.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.790
Oh my god I look so creepy saying that.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:19.183
So does that make me Professor X?

00:03:19.193 --> 00:03:20.252
- [Interviewer] Yes.

00:03:20.252 --> 00:03:21.203
- Thank you.

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.283
Call me professor T.

00:03:25.398 --> 00:03:26.231
(soft music)

00:03:26.231 --> 00:03:28.100
Little Mermaid is everything,

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.639
because morals and values
were built on Disney.

00:03:31.639 --> 00:03:34.330
Being in a world where you
think you have everything

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.265
and everyone tells you that you should,

00:03:36.265 --> 00:03:39.370
that you should believe
what they're saying

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:42.840
but you believe in a
bigger world and you go out

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:44.330
of your comfort zone for love

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:47.040
and I think that's an amazing story.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.300
And it's ironic 'cause
I'm scared of fish eyes.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.223
Weird, right?

00:03:50.850 --> 00:03:52.463
No side eyes though from Ariel.

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:54.530
(upbeat music)

00:03:54.530 --> 00:03:57.940
That's a hard question
because we love all of them.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:00.113
But I did get to meet Victoria Beckham.

00:04:00.290 --> 00:04:02.850
She told me about, she said,
yeah being in a girl band

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:04.500
is amazing, you create family from that.

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.952
And I was like, you're right.

00:04:06.952 --> 00:04:08.273
I love all of you.

00:04:08.420 --> 00:04:09.253
(laughs)

00:04:09.253 --> 00:04:10.086
Yes, I love them all.

00:04:10.969 --> 00:04:12.420
(playful music)

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:14.360
It was during their interview,
Taeyeon was like, yeah,

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:16.410
you need to go see her and she's like,

00:04:16.410 --> 00:04:17.910
I'm not that desperate.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:20.067
And it was a joke but
I guess the fans love

00:04:20.067 --> 00:04:23.350
when we say like pretty intense key words

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:26.063
and that's why they're like,
Taeyeon's not desperate.

00:04:26.140 --> 00:04:28.315
She posted a support post on my song.

00:04:28.315 --> 00:04:31.210
She put like every pink emoji there was

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.880
and that takes a lot of time and heart

00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.993
and then the fans are like,
yeah, totally desperate.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.970
I was like, no she just
loves me, we love each other.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.910
Yes, we are desperate for each other.

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:42.260
Does that clear everything?

00:04:42.599 --> 00:04:43.432
(laughs)

